# =====================================================\n# TESTS PACKAGE - All Test Files\n# =====================================================\n# This package contains all the automated test files\n#\n# WHAT ARE TESTS?\n# Tests are Python functions that:\n# - Set up a test scenario\n# - Perform actions (like clicking buttons, typing text)\n# - Verify expected results\n# - If expectations are not met, the test FAILS\n#\n# HOW TO RUN TESTS:\n# Open terminal and run:\n#   pytest tests/test_e2e_flow.py -v\n# \n# -v means \"verbose\" (shows detailed output)\n#\n# TESTS INCLUDED:\n# - test_e2e_flow.py: Full end-to-end user journey test\n#   This simulates a complete customer flow from browsing to checkout\n#\n# WHY SEPARATE FROM PAGE OBJECTS?\n# - Tests should describe WHAT you're testing (user journeys)\n# - Page objects describe HOW to test (technical details)\n# - This separation makes tests easier to read and understand\n
